  "raw": " and the video guide for Ocarina of Time (which gave it an honourable mention). Within my gaming group at school I was often the bearer of bad news about its lack of wide appeal among fans; however I found this difficulty in understanding data both flattering and motivating due to PMNN's belief that no amount of data backing up a given position would ever convince some people.\n\nTherefore, in order to disabuse them all of data's lack of affect on their decision making process it is rewarding for me to see peer reviewed research showing why the assertions they rejected were incorrect! It should have been cause for joy but instead those mainstream sources simply said: \"These polls are unscientific trash\" and the obvious aim here being to dishearten everyone not spending unnecessary time reading them all including me and the other gamers who'd never heard of data backing them all up anyway before; thus rendering these results as meaningless nonsense to PMNNers everywhere. Even worse than norm but certainly second worst...",
  "serialized": "and the video guide for Ocarina of Time (which gave it an honourable mention). Within my gaming group at school I was often the bearer of bad news about its lack of wide appeal among fans; however I found this difficulty in understanding data both flattering and motivating due to PMNN's belief that no amount of data backing up a given position would ever convince some people. Therefore, in order to disabuse them all of data's lack of affect on their decision making process it is rewarding for me to see peer reviewed research showing why the assertions they rejected were incorrect! It should have been cause for joy but instead those mainstream sources simply said: \"These polls are unscientific trash\" and the obvious aim here being to dishearten everyone not spending unnecessary time reading them all including me and the other gamers who'd never heard of data backing them all up anyway before; thus rendering these results as meaningless nonsense to PMNNers everywhere. Even worse than norm but certainly second worst...",
